playId":"401856741272","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0229,"playId":"401856741275","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0209,"playId":"401856741279","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0207,"playId":"401856741283","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0182,"playId":"401856741286","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0101,"playId":"401856741291","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0065,"playId":"401856741298","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0089,"playId":"401856741302","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0094,"playId":"401856741305","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0096,"playId":"401856741310","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0094,"playId":"401856741317","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0112,"playId":"401856741315","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0118,"playId":"401856741321","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.012,"playId":"401856741325","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0113,"playId":"401856741328","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3974","guid":"b66d33d7-3b2e-33d5-ac87-ba5e752596ca","fullName":"Vaught-Hemingway Stadium","address":{"city":"Oxford","state":"MS","zipCode":"38655","country":"USA"},"grass":true,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/3974.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]},{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/interior/3974.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day","interior"]}]},"attendance":68814},"article":{"headline":"Gunner Stockton and No. 2 Georgia pound No. 12 Mississippi 42-7 to make case for top ranking","description":"— Gunner Stockton passed for four touchdowns and ran for another Saturday night as No. 2 Georgia coasted to a 42-7 win over No. 12 Mississippi.","story":"OXFORD, Miss. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4685578/gunner-stockton\" target=\"_new\">Gunner Stockton</a> passed for four touchdowns and ran for another Saturday night as No. 2 Georgia coasted to a 42-7 win over No. 12 Mississippi.\n\n\r\n              Georgia (8-1, 6-1 Southeastern Conference, No. 2 CFP) dominated the opening 22 minutes with touchdown drives of 72, 96, 61 and 50 yards while Ole Miss crossed midfield once.\n\n\r\n              Stockton finished 9 of 15 passing for 186 yards, directing the Bulldogs to a 28-0 halftime lead. Georgia finished with 482 yards of offense, 298 in the first half.\n\n\r\n              The Bulldogs' impressive all-around performance could elevate them into the top spot in the AP Top 25 after <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/miami-notre-dame-score-college-football-dc2fecb79fcc40e4f2e1fb62fabec4b0\">No. 1 Miami lost at No. 4 Notre Dame</a>.\n\n\r\n              “A total team effort. I thought we embraced the challenge right from the start,” Georgia coach Kirby Smart said. “We talked about being the hunter and being aggressive and I thought we did that.”\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5141671/talyn-taylor\" target=\"_new\">Talyn Taylor</a> had touchdown receptions of 6, 58 and 65 yards, while <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5141371/ethan-barbour\" target=\"_new\">Ethan Barbour</a> had a 3-yard TD catch. Taylor finished with 140 yards on four receptions.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5263766/craig-dandridge\" target=\"_new\">Craig Dandridge</a> Jr. had a 4-yard touchdown run and Stockton rushed for a 15-yard score. The Bulldogs rushed for 295 yards, led by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5084047/nate-frazier\" target=\"_new\">Nate Frazier</a> with 107 yards on 16 carries.\n\n\r\n              Ole Miss (6-3, 4-3, No. 10 CFP) had its 16-game home winning streak snapped as Smart won in Oxford for the first time in three tries.\n\n\r\n              “That was a big-time win over a big-time team in a big-time environment,” Smart said. “We get to embrace it for 24 hours, then work to repeat it.”\n\n\r\n              The Rebels' <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4911529/trinidad-chambliss\" target=\"_new\">Trinidad Chambliss</a> went 18 of 34 passing for 170 yards but was sacked five times and threw an interception. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5214395/shekai-mills-knight\" target=\"_new\">Shekai Mills-Knight</a> scored on an 8-yard run for the Rebels, who were held to 252 yards of offense.\n\n\r\n              “It was surprising how poorly we started, it’s embarrassing,” Chambliss said. “We have to have a short memory about this.”\n\n\r\n              It was a stark contrast to the teams' two meetings last season, when Georgia won 43-35 at home and Ole Miss beat the Bulldogs 39-34 in a College Football Playoff quarterfinal at the Sugar Bowl.\n\n\r\n              “Georgia is a really good team but I did not see that butt-whipping coming,” Ole Miss coach Pete Golding said. “It was obvious that we (coaches) did not have the team ready to play.”\n\n\r\n              <hl2>The takeaway</hl2>\r\n              Georgia: The Bulldogs enhanced their CFP resume and strengthened their position at the top of the SEC standings. Linebacker <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/555721/chris-cole\" target=\"_new\">Chris Cole</a> led a dominant defensive performance with nine tackles, two quarterback hurries, 1 1/2 sacks and 1 1/2 tackles for loss.\n\n\r\n              Ole Miss: Despite a 3-3 record against ranked opponents, the Rebels remain in a logjam of SEC teams with similar two or three-loss resumes.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Poll implications</hl2>\r\n              Georgia will be a contender for the top spot in the AP poll and the CFP rankings, along with Notre Dame and unbeaten Utah.\n\n\r\n              “It means we are in the hunt for whatever,” safety <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079334/kj-bolden\" target=\"_new\">KJ Bolden</a> said. “This win means a lot.”\n\n\r\n              Ole Miss, meanwhile, must hope its third loss won't eliminate it from CFP consideration.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Georgia: Hosts No. 19 Missouri next Saturday.\n\n\r\n              Ole Miss: Visit Oklahoma next Saturday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              This story has been updated to correct Taylor, Barbour touchdown catch details.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here</a>.","published":"2026-11-08T04:33:34Z"}}